ue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Hello. I have code like below:\r\n\r\n```php\r\nprotected function getStatement(string $sql): PDOStatement\r\n{\r\n    $newPrepared = $this->pdoConnection->prepare($sql);\r\n    if (!($newPrepared instanceof PDOStatement)) {\r\n        throw new Exception(\"Can't prepare statement for {$sql}\");\r\n    }\r\n    return $newPrepared;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nPsalm throws a notice while checking `Found a redundant condition when evaluating $newPrepared and trying to reconcile type 'PDOStatement' to PDOStatement`. But I'm pretty sure that `prepare` method can returns a bool value depends on [error handling mode](http://php.net/manual/en/pdo.error-handling.php).\r\n\r\nLooks like related to https://github.com/vimeo/psalm/issues/669.\r\n\r\nAnyway i don't actually need this condition but other checker in my project wants to see it. I just want to understand which way is correct and which way i should use.\r\n\r\nPsalm version is `Psalm 2.0.17@ead7d62d489d58edb4fa03b21e4f0bc87a476211`.","closed_by":{"login":"muglug","id":2292638,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTI2Mzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2292638?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug","html_url":"https://github.com/muglug","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_ad